# Numbers With Same Consecutive Differences

[**967. Numbers With Same Consecutive Differences**](https://leetcode.com/problems/numbers-with-same-consecutive-differences/)

## Approach: Recursion + Backtracking

1. Use recursion to generate all possible numbers of length `n`.
2. Handle the leading digit separately because a number cannot start with `0`.
3. For every subsequent digit, check whether the absolute difference between the previous digit and the current digit is equal to `k`.
4. If the condition is satisfied, append the digit and make a recursive call.
5. After returning from recursion, remove the last digit using `pop_back()` to explore other possibilities.
6. When the length of the number becomes `n`, convert it into an integer and store it in the result.

## Code

```cpp
class Solution {
public:
    vector<int> result;

    void find_total_nums(string& num, int n, bool leading, int k) {
        if(num.length() == n) {
            result.push_back(stoi(num));
            return;
        }

        int start = (leading) ? 1 : 0;

        for(int i = start; i <= 9; i++) {
            if(leading) {
                num += (i + '0');
                find_total_nums(num, n, false, k);
                num.pop_back();
            }
            else {
                int n1 = num.back() - '0';
                int curr = i;

                if(abs(n1 - curr) == k) {
                    num += (i + '0');
                    find_total_nums(num, n, false, k);
                    num.pop_back();
                }
            }
        }
    }

    vector<int> numsSameConsecDiff(int n, int k) {
        result.clear();

        string num = "";
        bool leading = true;

        find_total_nums(num, n, leading, k);

        return result;
    }
};
```

## Complexity Analysis

- **Time Complexity:** \(O(10 \times 2^{n-1} \times n)\) — At most 9 starting digits and 2 possible choices for each subsequent digit (when \(k > 0\)). Each completed number takes \(O(n)\) time to convert using `stoi()`.
- **Space Complexity:** \(O(n)\) — Recursion depth and the temporary string require \(O(n)\) auxiliary space, excluding the output vector.

